INSERT INTO table2 (c4, c1) VALUES (500, 1);
INSERT INTO table2 (c4, c1) VALUES (500, 2);

/*
Explanation of the result:
 • Q1: SELECT A.c4, ROUND(AVG(B.c2), 2) … GROUP BY A.c4 will use table2.c4 (which is 500 for every row) so it returns one row: 500 and average (10+30)/2 = 20.00.
 • Q2: SELECT c4, ROUND(AVG(c2), 2) … GROUP BY c4, if the unqualified c4 now is resolved to table1.c4 (because table1 also has a c4 column), then it will group by 1 and 2 separately and return two rows with averages 10 and 30 respectively.
Thus the two queries will yield different results under this counterexample.
*/

