-- For the row with c5=1, table2 contains ('T2_a','T2_b') while table1 contains ('T1_x','T1_y') along with extra columns ('T1_extra1','T1_extra2').
-- In Q1 the intended design is honored because the SELECT list (c3, c4, c2, c6) unambiguously means table2.c3, table2.c4, table1.c2, table1.c6, so the row will be:
--      T2_a, T2_b, T1_x, T1_y
