-- Now, if you were to delete the TABLE1 row for c2 = 1 (i.e. remove the matching row), then:
--    • In Q1, the TABLE2 row with c2 = 1 would appear (because table1.c1 becomes NULL and the IS NULL check passes),
--    • In Q2, the TABLE2 row with c2 = 1 would appear as well because COALESCE(NULL,0)=0 and 0 < 1000 is true.

